 [" ic", -10.683822631835938]]}, {"t": "ic", "lp": -4.22009798057843e-05, "top": [["ic", -4.22009798057843e-05], [" ic", -10.791299819946289]]}, {"t": "px", "lp": -0.00020094744104426354, "top": [["px", -0.00020094744104426354], ["PX", -10.707581520080566]]}, {"t": "`", "lp": -0.0005133277154527605, "top": [["`", -0.0005133277154527605], [" `", -10.236169815063477]]}, {"t": " |", "lp": -0.0003299065283499658, "top": [[" |", -0.0003299065283499658], ["|", -10.768936157226562]]}, {"t": " Use", "lp": -0.0004975841147825122, "top": [[" Use", -0.0004975841147825122], [" Intel", -8.375480651855469]]}, {"t": " Intel", "lp": -0.0003551875415723771, "top": [[" Intel", -0.0003551875415723771], ["Intel", -8.30402946472168]]}, {"t": "'s", "lp": -0.00016964921087492257, "top": [["'s", -0.00016964921087492257], ["\u7684", -9.086346626281738]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. Without this, `icx`/`icpx` wouldn't be found.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero status (an error). A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into confusing downstream errors.\n\n## The CMake Invocation\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag by flag:\n\n| Flag | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` | **Source directory** \u2014 where the source code lives (the git clone). |\n| `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` | **Build directory** \u2014 where build artifacts go (out-of-source build). |\n| `-G Ninja` | Use the **Ninja** build generator (fast, minimal syntax). |\n| `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release` | Optimize build with `-O3`-level optimizations, no debug symbols. |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr` | Where `make install` will place files (system root). |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib` | Put libraries in `/usr/lib` (not `/usr/lib64`). |\n| `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx` | Use Intel's **C** compiler (icx) instead of gcc. |\n| `-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx` | Use Intel's"}